# Binary assets are forbidden by constitution II. This ignore list is that rule
# enforced at the tooling layer: an agent cannot accidentally `git add` a texture it
# was told not to create. Exceptions must be deliberate and reviewed.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.bmp
*.mp3
*.wav
*.ogg
*.m4a
*.glb
*.gltf
*.fbx
*.obj
*.ttf
*.otf
*.woff
*.woff2

node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

test-results/
playwright-report/

.DS_Store
.env
.env.*

# Ergane runtime root: worktrees, session transcripts, verification evidence.
.ergane/

# Ergane's worktree-boundary detector writes its findings here, inside the repo it
# audits. Untracked and unignored, it appears as `git status` noise and is one
# `git add -A` from being committed. See feedback #48.
.ergane-detector/

# Ergane's verification store: a live SQLite database (verification.db plus its
# -wal and -shm sidecars) that the worker writes while gates run. Untracked and
# unignored it is one `git add -A` from being committed mid-write, which commits
# a torn database. Same hazard as .ergane-detector/ above.
.factory/
